#!/bin/sh

# Nothing to generate on a box that is not part of a mesh.
#
# This runs once, at first boot - before anyone has decided what the box is
# for. The hotplug handler beside it (11-multiap-genconfig) has carried this
# gate since 2026-08-17; this file did not, and that alone was enough to undo
# it. Measured the same day on a freshly flashed production image: no role, no
# dhcp.lan.ignore, every mesh worker disabled, and the board still came up
# broadcasting 'OpenWrt-' and 'MAP--BH' instead of the OpenWrt-2g/5g/6g
# networks it is meant to offer. Gating one caller and not the other gates
# nothing.
#
# The three tests below are deliberately identical to the hotplug handler's,
# where the reasoning for each of them is written out in full. Only the last
# word differs, and has to: that file is sourced, so it says return; this one
# is executed, so it says exit.
#
# In short: /etc/mapc/role is what easymesh-role writes before it touches
# anything else, and /etc/easymesh-wps-pending covers a join in progress,
# whose config has to be built before the role exists. If one of them
# changes, both files change together.
#
# Exiting here removes this script, and that is correct: it is a first-boot
# default, not a policy. A box that later becomes a mesh node has the hotplug
# handler, which fires on every radio at every boot, and easymesh-role, which
# builds the configuration itself when a role is assigned.
#
# 2026-08-17, later the same day: dhcp.lan.ignore was removed from this test.
# It had been included as the mark carried by nodes configured before
# /etc/mapc/role existed. It cannot serve that purpose - easymesh-dhcp-safe
# writes dhcp.lan.ignore='1' on every box that is not a controller, factory ones
# included, so the mark appeared on untouched routers and reopened this gate one
# boot later. Three builds in a row came up with a backhaul on the air because of
# it. Older nodes now get the real marker from 88-easymesh-role-marker instead.
#
# A mark only means "someone decided" if nothing but a decision can produce it.
[ -f /etc/mapc/role ] ||
	[ -f /etc/easymesh-wps-pending ] || exit 0

/lib/wifi/multiap conf
